    "title": "Who plays in MLB today? Opening Day schedule for all 30 teams",
    "text": "March 25, 2026Updated March 26, 2026, 9:51 a.m. ETThe wait is over. Baseball is back.The 2026 Major League Baseball began Wednesday with a standalone contest between the New York Yankees and San Francisco Giants that streamed exclusively on Netflix.The Yankees cruised to a 7-0 victory on Opening Night thanks to a five-run second inning and a strong outing from ace Max Fried despite captain Aaron Judge, the reigning American League MVP, being the only player that went hitless in the lineup as he finished 0-for-5 with four strikeouts.The remaining 28 clubs will get their seasons underway over the course of the next two days, with 22 teams, including the New York Mets, having first pitch on Thursday, March 26.Watch Yankees regular-season games on FuboTVOpening Day will continue on Friday, March 27, with the final six teams making their debut for the 2026 regular season.Here's are important details you need to know for Opening Day across Major League Baseball:(All times Eastern):MLB Opening Day 2026 schedule, starting pitchers revealedHere's the Opening Day schedule for all 30 teams along with the corresponding starting pitcher for each club in their 2026 opener:Wednesday, March 25Yankees 7, Giants 0Thursday, March 26Pittsburgh Pirates (Paul Skenes) at New York Mets (Freddy Peralta), 1:15 p.m.Chicago White Sox (Shane Smith) at Milwaukee Brewers (Jacob Misiorowski), 2:10 p.m.Washington Nationals (Cade Cavalli) at Chicago Cubs (Matthew Boyd), 2:20 p.m.Minnesota Twins (Joe Ryan) at Baltimore Orioles (Trevor Rogers), 3:05 p.m.Boston Red Sox (Garrett Crochet) at Cincinnati Reds (Andrew Abbott), 4:10 p.m.Los Angeles Angels (Jose Soriano) at Houston Astros (Hunter Brown), 4:10 p.m.Detroit Tigers (Tarik Skubal) at San Diego Padres (Nick Pivetta), 4:10 p.m.Texas Rangers (Nathan Eovaldi) at Philadelphia Phillies (Cristopher Sanchez), 4:15 p.m.Tampa Bay Rays (Drew Rasmussen) at St. Louis Cardinals (Matthew Liberatore), 4:15 p.m.Arizona Diamondbacks (Zac Gallen) at Los Angeles Dodgers (Yoshinobu Yamamoto), 8:30 p.m.Cleveland Guardians (Tanner Bibee) at Seattle Mariners (Logan Gilbert), 10:10 p.m.Friday, March 27Athletics (Luis Severino) at Toronto Blue Jays (Kevin Gausman), 7:07 p.m.Colorado Rockies (Kyle Freeland) at Miami Marlins (Sandy Alcantara), 7:10 p.m.Kansas City Royals (Cole Ragans) at Atlanta Braves (Chris Sale), 7:15 p.m.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
